  "revision": {
    "title": "Quick Revision — Lesson V (Dative)",
    "summaryHtml": "The Dative (-āya/-ssa sg., -ānaṃ pl.) marks the <strong>recipient</strong> or <strong>purpose</strong>: \"for the hermit,\" \"to the teacher.\"",
    "connectionHtml": "<strong>Connection:</strong> The Dative and Genitive share the <em>same plural ending</em> (-ānaṃ) and one singular ending (-ssa). Context tells you which case is meant. The Genitive shows <em>possession</em> — \"of the man.\"",
    "questions": [
      {
        "q": "What is the Dative plural ending?",
        "a": "<strong>-ānaṃ</strong>"
      },
      {
        "q": "\"The farmer brings rice for the hermit\" → Pāli?",
        "a": "<strong>Kassako tāpasāya bhattaṃ āharati</strong>"
      }
    ]
  },
  "teach": [
    {
      "id": "grammar",
      "title": "The Genitive CasePossession",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 2,
          "eyebrow": "Grammar",
          "html": "The <em>Genitive</em> Case<br>Possession"
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "html": "The Genitive case shows <strong>possession or relationship</strong>. It translates as <em>\"of\"</em> or <em>\"'s\"</em> in English."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "html": "The Genitive is one of the simplest cases. Its endings overlap with the Dative: <strong>-ssa</strong> (sg.) and <strong>-ānaṃ</strong> (pl.). Context tells them apart — Genitive = \"of,\" Dative = \"for.\""
        },
        {
          "type": "rule",
          "title": "For masculine nouns ending in -a:",
          "formulas": [
            "Singular: base + <em>-ssa</em> <span>|</span> narassa = <em>of the man</em>",
            "Plural:&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;base + <em>-ānaṃ</em> <span>|</span> narānaṃ = <em>of men</em>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "caption": "Six cases so far",
          "head": [
            "Case",
            "Function",
            "Singular",
            "Plural"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Nominative",
              "Subject",
              "<span class=\"decl-ending\">-o</span>",
              "<span class=\"decl-ending\">-ā</span>"
            ],
            [
              "Accusative",
              "Object",
              "<span class=\"decl-ending\">-ṃ</span>",
              "<span class=\"decl-ending\">-e</span>"
            ],
            [
              "Instrumental",
              "By/with",
              "<span class=\"decl-ending\">-ena</span>",
              "<span class=\"decl-ending\">-ehi</span>"
            ],
            [
              "Ablative",
              "From",
              "<span class=\"decl-ending\">-ā/-smā/-mhā</span>",
              "<span class=\"decl-ending\">-ehi</span>"
            ],
            [
              "Dative",
              "For/to",
              "<span class=\"decl-ending\">-āya/-ssa</span>",
              "<span class=\"decl-ending\">-ānaṃ</span>"
            ],
            [
              "Genitive",
              "Of",
              "<span class=\"decl-ending\">-ssa</span>",
              "<span class=\"decl-ending\">-ānaṃ</span>"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
